{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00339",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.09,
      "end_seconds": 3.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Good morning. Come in, have a seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.1,
      "end_seconds": 7.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. Thanks for seeing me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.0,
      "end_seconds": 12.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Doctor, um, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.61,
      "end_seconds": 19.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. Did the receptionist sort you out quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.66,
      "end_seconds": 24.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, she was lovely about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.06,
      "end_seconds": 26.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "So, how have things been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.87,
      "end_seconds": 35.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "Yeah, um, he's been having severe pain in my right side that comes in waves, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.7,
      "end_seconds": 43.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.66,
      "end_seconds": 55.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.04,
      "text": "Oh, you know, I'd say moderate. It's a couple of times a week. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.78,
      "end_seconds": 59.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Okay, does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.41,
      "end_seconds": 72.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.28,
      "text": "Pain moving down to the groin goes along with it, most of the time. I've also had blood in the urine, for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.18,
      "end_seconds": 77.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Any restlessness, you can't sit still as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.86,
      "end_seconds": 86.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Yes, for about a week. The pain moving down to the groin? That's been for three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 87.39,
      "end_seconds": 90.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.45,
      "end_seconds": 94.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Okay, so yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.43,
      "end_seconds": 97.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "And fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.82,
      "end_seconds": 101.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Hmm, not at all, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 102.28,
      "end_seconds": 106.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.73,
      "end_seconds": 113.77,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Um, no, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.46,
      "end_seconds": 121.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Have you had any vomiting, previous kidney stones or testicular pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.11,
      "end_seconds": 125.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, no. None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.83,
      "end_seconds": 128.67,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.55,
      "end_seconds": 131.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 136.05,
      "end_seconds": 144.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Blood pressure 126 over 86, pulse 113. Oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature is 36.5 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.75,
      "end_seconds": 153.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.58,
      "end_seconds": 156.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Hmm, my mother has migraines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.16,
      "end_seconds": 161.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.88,
      "end_seconds": 187.33,
      "duration_seconds": 24.45,
      "text": "Hmm, I have high blood pressure, for two years. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know. I've got gout. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I mean, um, I have asthma, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.34,
      "end_seconds": 190.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.07,
      "end_seconds": 212.22,
      "duration_seconds": 17.15,
      "text": "Hmm, you know, not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.97,
      "end_seconds": 214.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Alright, any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.95,
      "end_seconds": 220.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.79,
      "end_seconds": 239.22,
      "duration_seconds": 17.43,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.81,
      "end_seconds": 243.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Oh, I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.54,
      "end_seconds": 248.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.93,
      "end_seconds": 252.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Yes, um, I'm allergic to aspirin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.36,
      "end_seconds": 255.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "What about operations, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.29,
      "end_seconds": 261.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Yes, I had my thyroid operated on, a long time ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.02,
      "end_seconds": 275.53,
      "duration_seconds": 13.51,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.19,
      "end_seconds": 279.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Thank you, you know, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.01,
      "end_seconds": 285.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.06,
      "end_seconds": 290.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Losartan. I take it 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 293.39,
      "end_seconds": 300.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the losartan was 25 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.46,
      "end_seconds": 305.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.52,
      "end_seconds": 318.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "Uh, I don't think I have it with me. It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.34,
      "end_seconds": 323.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Right, do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 324.18,
      "end_seconds": 330.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.17,
      "end_seconds": 336.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.49,
      "end_seconds": 338.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.44,
      "end_seconds": 341.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Let me press here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.15,
      "end_seconds": 359.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the right loin when I tap, and your tummy is soft."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.93,
      "end_seconds": 360.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.73,
      "end_seconds": 380.23,
      "duration_seconds": 17.5,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.02,
      "end_seconds": 383.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.1,
      "end_seconds": 397.5,
      "duration_seconds": 13.4,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like a kidney stone. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I'd also keep a urine infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.92,
      "end_seconds": 402.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Um, should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 403.72,
      "end_seconds": 419.55,
      "duration_seconds": 15.83,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a kidney stone is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had severe pain in your right side that comes in waves, moderate, and no testicular pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 422.55,
      "end_seconds": 423.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.04,
      "end_seconds": 446.85,
      "duration_seconds": 21.81,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a urine test for flank pain. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm going to order kidney function tests, for renal colic. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'll start you on paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed, for three days. That's for pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 447.28,
      "end_seconds": 450.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Okay, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 454.0,
      "end_seconds": 479.21,
      "duration_seconds": 25.21,
      "text": "Drink three litres of water a day and try to strain your urine so we can catch the stone if it passes. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. If you smoke, this is a good moment to think about stopping, and we can help you with that. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 479.76,
      "end_seconds": 481.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 482.5,
      "end_seconds": 491.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you get a fever or can't pass urine at all. Come back after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 491.77,
      "end_seconds": 492.47,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 493.02,
      "end_seconds": 497.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Okay, summarise it for me, what's the plan from your side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 498.49,
      "end_seconds": 508.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.07,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 1 gram, every six hours if needed and come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 509.79,
      "end_seconds": 513.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 515.51,
      "end_seconds": 519.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    }
  ]
}